From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Moraza Sanchez <dmorazasanchezmendo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] radv,aco,nir: BC-250 FSR4 deferred SDot lowering
 (EXP-042B / V3)

Supersedes the earlier unconditional/selective reassociation of
sdot_4x8_a_b (EXP-028 / v2). V3 fuses FSR4's iadd(0, OpSDot) wrapper
before the software fallback, defers remaining GFX1013 compute SDot
operations through one NIR optimization round before restoring the
real capability set and lowering to software, and adds ACO support
for the signed i24 MAD form and GFX1013-only dense-reduction/two-chain
lowering for pressure-sensitive shaders.

A 64-shader FSR4 capture found register pressure and occupancy, not
static instruction count, are what actually govern runtime: the
previously pathological ED7 shader drops from 1314 VGPR spills / 4
waves per SIMD to 0 spills / 6 waves per SIMD under V3, despite a
higher naive inverse-cost estimate. Tested end to end with FSR 4.1.1
in Cyberpunk 2077 at 63 FPS, up from 58 FPS pre-V3.

This is EXP-042B from BC-250 FSR4 testing (David Moraza Sanchez,
dmorazasanchez/bc250-fsr4, `v3` branch,
https://github.com/dmorazasanchez/bc250-fsr4/tree/v3).

The GFX1013 compute-queue/identity changes and the RADV_GFX103
opt-in override that ship inside upstream's bc250-fsr4-v3.patch are
intentionally omitted here: they duplicate 0001 and 0004 byte-for-byte
and are already applied by those patches.
